# ============================================================
#  Rivalry (world expansion 1, plan §2b): Lyra and Bram, the two written rivals, get a rivalry worth
#  having (eight cards each, with the generic truce no longer pre-empting them: migration 0040); Corvin
#  and Ilse, who are never rivals, get two cards each for when things have soured.
#  Lyra's way out is lyra_rival_respect; Bram's is bram_turns, opened by bram_crying or bram_steps_in.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Lyra ----------------

@event lyra_rankings_war
title: The Rankings War
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: bond(lyra) == "rival" and term
repeat: 3
weight: 10
art: book
tags: rival study
scene: A noticeboard outside the Great Hall with the term's rankings pinned up, two names side by side at the top, a red-haired student tapping one with her wand.
text: The rankings are up outside the Great Hall. {~You're one place above Lyra.|Lyra is one place above you.} She's standing in front of the list when you get there, and she doesn't move aside. "Enjoy it," she says. "It's the last time."
> left: Out-study her this term
  study +medium
  health -small
  rel lyra -tiny
  say: {~You take the library table opposite hers and don't leave it for a month. She doesn't either. Thorne remarks that he's never seen the library so tense. The next list has you in the same order. Neither of you is satisfied.|You study every night. So does she; you can see her lamp from your window. It's the best work either of you has done, and you'd both rather die than say so.}
> right: Leave a note on her desk
  mood +small
  renown +tiny
  rel lyra -small
  say: {~"Second suits you." She finds it in front of the whole class, and goes the colour of her hair. The next morning there's a note on yours: "Says the person who'll be third."|You leave a single word: "Close." It drives her mad for a week. It was meant to.}

@pool rivals_lyra_social_routine
actor: lyra
trigger: social
class: routine
weight: 10
tags: rival

@event lyra_sabotage_returned
title: Pink Bubbles, Returned
pool: rivals_lyra_social_routine
tone: tense
when: bond(lyra) == "rival" and chosen(lyra_rival_sabotage, left)
art: potion
scene: A student's wand producing a cloud of blue smoke shaped like a donkey in the middle of a lecture, a red-haired student three rows away not looking.
text: In the middle of Thorne's lecture your wand produces a cloud of blue smoke shaped like a donkey. Three rows away, Lyra is taking very careful notes. It's your move. It's always your move.
> left: Call a ceasefire
  rel lyra +small
  mood -small
  say: You slip her a note: "Truce? I'm running out of eyebrows." She reads it twice, and writes underneath: "Truce. For now. The donkey was very good though." It was.
> right: Escalate
  challenge deceive vs lyra.guile:
    win:
      renown +small
      rel lyra -small
      say: Her next spell comes out as a choir of tiny frogs singing her family motto. The whole class applauds. Lyra stands there with her wand out, absolutely white, and then, unbelievably, starts to laugh.
    lose:
      gain detention
      rel lyra -small
      say: She sees it coming a mile off and turns it round. You spend detention scrubbing cauldrons. She spends it in the next room, also scrubbing cauldrons, for the donkey.

@event lyra_glove_thrown
title: The Glove Thrown
pool: rivals_lyra_social_routine
tone: tense
when: bond(lyra) == "rival" and rel(lyra) <= 0
art: duel
tags: danger
scene: A white duelling glove on the flagstones of a crowded courtyard, a red-haired student standing over it with her wand drawn, a ring of watching students.
text: Lyra drops a glove at your feet in the courtyard, in front of everyone. "The ring. Tonight. No referee but the crowd." She's been waiting for this all term. So, if you're honest, have you.
> left: Leave the glove where it lies
  renown -small
  rel lyra -tiny
  say: You step over it. The crowd mutters. Lyra picks it up herself, very slowly. "Next time," she says. "There's always a next time." There is.
> right: Pick it up
  challenge combat vs lyra.arcana +1:
    win:
      renown +large
      rel lyra +small
      say: You win, barely, in front of half the school. Lyra gets up off the flagstones and, after a long moment, holds out the glove. "Keep it," she says. "Until I win it back."
    lose:
      health -medium
      renown +small
      say: She wins, and it costs her: she's limping, and she knows you made her work for every point. "Good," she says, breathing hard. "Good. Again, soon."

@event lyra_allies_thornwick
title: Allies, for an Afternoon
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: (bond(lyra) == "rival" or rel(lyra) <= -6) and seen(life_rival_academy) > 0 and around(lyra)
weight: 9
art: flame
tags: rival
scene: Two rival students standing shoulder to shoulder in a corridor facing a group of visitors in green Thornwick colours, both wands half-drawn.
text: Three Thornwick students in green are laughing at the Lumenhold crest in the entrance hall. Lyra hears it at the same moment you do. She looks at you. You look at her. For the first time all year, you're on the same side.
> left: Stand with her
  rel lyra +medium
  health -tiny
  say: You stand shoulder to shoulder. The Thornwick students take one look at the two of you and remember an appointment elsewhere, though the last one flicks a jinx at your ankles on the way out, and it stings for an hour. Lyra doesn't thank you. She does walk with you as far as the stairs, which is unheard of.
> right: Let her handle it
  study +small
  rel lyra -tiny
  say: You leave her to it and get an hour's reading done in the library. She handles it alone, magnificently, and you hear about it at dinner from four different people. "You missed it," she says, passing. She sounds as if she minds.

@event lyra_mother_watches
title: Her Mother Watches You Win
pool: rivals_lyra_social_routine
tone: tense
when: bond(lyra) == "rival" and year >= 2
art: duel
scene: An exhibition duelling ring with a gallery above, an elegant woman in black watching a red-haired student who is losing.
text: An exhibition bout, and you're paired with Lyra. Up in the gallery, in black, is Lady Vaneshade. Halfway through, you're winning, clearly, and Lyra knows it, and you see her glance up once at the gallery and then not again.
> left: Win it
  renown +medium
  rel lyra -small
  say: You win cleanly. The gallery applauds. Lady Vaneshade doesn't. She leaves before the bows. Lyra watches her go, and then turns and shakes your hand properly. "Don't you dare go easy on me," she says. "Ever." You won't.
> right: Let her come back
  rel lyra +medium
  renown -small
  alignment +tiny
  say: You slow down, just enough. Lyra wins. In the gallery, her mother nods once. Afterwards Lyra corners you, furious. "You let me," she says. Then, so quietly you nearly miss it: "Thank you. Never again."

@event lyra_rival_letter
title: A Rival's Letter
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: letter
actor: lyra
when: bond(lyra) == "rival" and break
repeat: 6
weight: 10
art: letter
tags: rival letter
scene: A letter with a black Vaneshade seal on a windowsill, inside it a neatly ruled table of marks with one line underlined twice.
text: A letter with the Vaneshade seal. Inside: a ruled table of her term marks, beside yours, with every subject she beat you in underlined. {~At the bottom: "Enjoy your holiday. I'm not taking one."|At the bottom: "You're welcome to check my sums. They're right."}
> left: Write back with corrections
  lore +small
  rel lyra +small
  mood -tiny
  say: {~You find one mistake in her sums, in your favour, and write back about it at length. Her reply is two words: "Noted. Grrr."|You send back her table with your own column added: hours slept. She doesn't answer for a week. Then: "Fine. I'll sleep. Some."}
> right: Pin it above your desk
  mood +small
  study +tiny
  say: {~You pin it up where you'll see it every morning. It works better than any timetable.|Up it goes, above your desk. Every time you want to stop, there it is, underlined twice.}

@event lyra_last_match
title: The Last Rankings
class: routine
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: bond(lyra) == "rival" and final_year and month >= 6
weight: 12
art: book
tags: rival
scene: A final rankings list on a noticeboard, two names tied at the top, two students standing in front of it in silence.
text: The last rankings you'll ever see at Lumenhold. You and Lyra are tied. Exactly. She stands in front of the list for a long time. "Four years," she says. "And it comes to that." She doesn't sound angry. She sounds almost happy.
> left: Share it
  rel lyra +large
  renown -tiny
  say: "Joint," you say. She looks at you, and then holds out her hand. You shake. "It was never going to be anyone else," she says. "I'm glad it was you I didn't beat."
  if knows(lyra.mother):
    rel lyra +tiny
    say: Then you say "well done", because somebody should, once. She doesn't answer. She holds on to your hand a moment longer.
> right: Ask Thorne for a decider
  challenge research expert-:
    win:
      renown +medium
      rel lyra +small
      say: Thorne sets you both one question, the hardest he has. You get it by a hair. Lyra reads your answer, and nods, and says, "That's right. That's annoyingly right." She's proud of you. She'll never say it.
    lose:
      renown +small
      rel lyra +small
      say: Thorne sets you both one question. She gets it. You don't. She doesn't gloat, which is how you know she means it when she says, "Thank you. That's the only one I wanted."

# ---------------- Bram ----------------

@event bram_marked
title: Top of the Ledger
class: milestone
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: bram
when: year == 1 and month >= 2 and month <= 3 and bond(bram) == "none" and rel(bram) <= -12
weight: 14
art: shield
tags: rival
scene: A big student in a red prefect's sash writing a name at the top of a demerit ledger with great ceremony, another student watching from a doorway.
text: Bram opens his demerit ledger in the middle of the corridor and writes your name at the top of a fresh page, slowly, so you can watch him do it. "A page of your own," he says. "You've earned it."
> left: Keep your head down
  rel bram +small
  mood -small
  say: You walk past without a word. He looks almost disappointed. The page stays empty for a while. It doesn't stay empty for long.
> right: Meet his eye
  bond bram rival
  renown +tiny
  rel bram -tiny
  say: You stop, and look at him, and don't look away. "Good," says Bram, and snaps the ledger shut. "I was hoping you would." It's war, and you're both, somehow, pleased about it.

@event bram_demerit_ledger
title: The Demerit Ledger
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: bram
when: bond(bram) == "rival" or bond(bram) == "nemesis"
repeat: 3
weight: 10
art: shield
tags: rival
scene: A prefect's ledger open on a windowsill, a column of demerits next to one name, each with a reason in neat block capitals.
text: Bram has given you a demerit for {~"walking in a smug manner".|"breathing in a provocative direction".} It's the fourth this month. The ledger is starting to look like a novel.
> left: Accept it with dignity
  mood -small
  alignment +tiny
  say: {~You thank him for his diligence. He has no idea what to do with that. He writes "THANKED ME" in the margin, puzzled.|You nod gravely and walk on. He follows you for a corridor, waiting for you to crack. You don't.}
  if knows(bram.hall_tax):
    rel bram +tiny
    say: As you go, you add that at least it isn't a hall tax. He goes red to the ears.
> right: Appeal it to his face
  challenge appeal journeyman:
    win:
      renown +tiny
      rel bram -tiny
      say: {~You point out, with diagrams, that it's impossible to walk smugly. A crowd gathers. Bram crosses it out to make you stop.|You argue it so well that two first-years applaud. Bram crosses it out, then gives you a fresh one for "public speaking".}
    lose:
      gain detention
      say: {~"Arguing with a prefect," Bram says happily, writing. "That's a detention." It is.|You argue, and he writes, and the demerit becomes a detention. "Thank you," he says. "That's my quota."}

@pool rivals_bram_social_routine
actor: bram
trigger: social
class: routine
weight: 9
tags: rival

@event bram_inspection
title: Inspection
pool: rivals_bram_social_routine
tone: tense
when: bond(bram) == "rival" or bond(bram) == "nemesis"
art: shield
scene: A big prefect going through a student's dormitory trunk with exaggerated care, holding up a sock with two fingers, the owner standing in the doorway.
text: "Room inspection," Bram announces, at your door, with a clipboard. There is no such thing as room inspection. He's already in. He's already opening your trunk.
> left: Let him search
  mood -small
  chance unlikely:
    gain detention
    say: He finds the kitchen's missing jar of honey under your bed. You have no idea how it got there. He does, you suspect. Detention.
  else:
    rel bram +tiny
    say: He finds nothing worse than socks. He's almost disappointed. On his way out he straightens your books, without thinking, and then glares at you as if you made him do it.
> right: Inspect him back
  challenge deceive vs bram.guile:
    win:
      renown +small
      rel bram -small
      say: While he's in your trunk, you inspect his clipboard. It's mostly a drawing of a horse, quite good. You hold it up for the corridor to see. He leaves. Quickly.
    lose:
      rel bram -small
      gain detention
      say: He catches you reading his clipboard. "Interfering with an inspection," he says. "Detention." He covers the clipboard with his hand as he goes.

@event bram_rumour
title: The Rumour He Started
pool: rivals_bram_social_routine
tone: tense
when: (bond(bram) == "rival" or bond(bram) == "nemesis") and renown >= 10
art: paper
scene: Students whispering behind their hands in a corridor as one student passes, a big prefect at the far end leaning on a wall, looking innocent.
text: There's a rumour going round that you cried at the Sorting Mirror. There's a rumour that you're afraid of owls. People are being very nice to you about the owls. You know exactly where it started.
> left: Rise above it
  renown -small
  mood -tiny
  say: You let it run. It dies in a fortnight, as rumours do. Bram looks faintly cheated. You catch him later telling a first-year that the owl one wasn't true, quite firmly.
> right: Start one back
  alignment -tiny
  renown +tiny
  rel bram -medium
  say: By Friday the whole school believes Bram sleeps with a night-light shaped like a duck. He doesn't deny it fast enough. It is, it turns out, true.

@event bram_hall_tax_escalated
title: The Hall Tax, Escalated
pool: rivals_bram_social_routine
tone: tense
when: knows(bram.hall_tax) and rel(bram) < 0 and not flag(bram_softened)
art: coin
scene: A big prefect standing at the foot of a second staircase with a collecting tin, a hand-lettered sign beside him reading WEST STAIRS, a queue of first-years.
text: The hall tax has spread. There's a tin at the foot of the west stairs now, too, and a hand-lettered sign, and Bram behind it looking enormously pleased with himself. A queue of first-years are emptying their pockets.
> left: Pay, and the first-years' too
  gold -small
  alignment +tiny
  rel bram -tiny
  say: You drop in enough for the whole queue. The first-years look at you like you've slain a dragon. Bram looks at the tin, and at you, and for some reason shuts it. The sign is gone the next day.
> right: Organise a boycott
  challenge appeal journeyman:
    win:
      renown +small
      rel bram -small
      say: By lunch, nobody in the castle is using the west stairs. They're using the windows, a laundry chute and, in one case, a broom. Bram stands by his empty tin until dinner. Then he quietly takes the sign down.
    lose:
      mood -small
      rel bram -tiny
      say: Nobody joins your boycott. The stairs are the shortest way to lunch. Bram waves at you, cheerfully, from behind his tin.

@event bram_after_curfew
title: Caught After Curfew
pool: rivals_bram_social_routine
tone: tense
when: bond(bram) == "rival" or bond(bram) == "nemesis"
time: night
art: candle
scene: A dark castle corridor at night, a lantern held high by a big prefect, a student caught halfway up a staircase.
text: Bram's lantern catches you halfway up the north stairs, an hour after curfew. He smiles, slowly. He's been waiting all year for this. "Well," he says. "Well, well, well."
> left: Take the detention
  gain detention
  rel bram +tiny
  say: "Fair," you say. It throws him; he'd prepared a speech. He writes you up. Then, as you go, he says, "Use the east stairs next time. They don't creak." You decide not to wonder why he told you.
> right: Talk your way past
  challenge deceive vs bram.guile:
    win:
      guile +small
      rel bram -small
      say: You tell him Professor Vey sent you for a book. He doesn't believe you. But he can't prove it, and he's not brave enough to ask Vey. He lets you go, fuming.
    lose:
      gain detention
      rel bram -small
      say: You try a story about sleepwalking. He lets you finish. Then he writes you up for curfew and for "insulting my intelligence", which he underlines.

@event bram_rematch
title: The Rematch
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: bram
when: (bond(bram) == "rival" or bond(bram) == "nemesis") and flag(beat_bram_duel)
weight: 10
art: duel
tags: rival danger
scene: The duelling green at dusk, a big student in a prefect's sash pulling on his gloves, a crowd forming a ring around him.
text: Bram has been practising. Everyone knows; you've heard him on the duelling green every evening for a month. Tonight he's waiting for you there. "Last time doesn't count," he says. "Again. Properly."
> left: Not tonight
  renown -tiny
  rel bram -tiny
  say: "Scared," says Bram, but he doesn't sound sure. He practises alone until dark. You can hear him from your window.
> right: Accept
  challenge combat vs bram.vigor +1:
    win:
      renown +medium
      rel bram +small
      say: He's better. Much better. You win anyway, by one exchange. He lies on the grass looking at the sky for a while. "A month," he says. "A whole month." Then he laughs, and you help him up, and he doesn't let go of your hand at once.
    lose:
      health -medium
      rel bram +small
      say: He wins. He stands over you, breathing hard, and doesn't gloat, and holds out a hand. "Now we're even," he says. "Now it's interesting."

@event bram_steps_in
title: He Steps In
pool: rivals_bram_social_routine
tone: tense
when: (bond(bram) == "rival" or bond(bram) == "nemesis") and not flag(bram_softened)
art: shield
scene: A big prefect standing between two older students and a frightened first-year at the boathouse, another student arriving at a run.
text: Two fourth-years have a first-year backed against the boathouse wall. Before you can move, Bram is there, between them, sash and all. "Problem?" he says. There are two of them, and they're bigger. He doesn't step aside.
> left: Stand beside him
  flag bram_softened
  health -tiny
  alignment +tiny
  rel bram +medium
  say: You step up next to him. One of them shoves you into the wall for form's sake, and then they decide it isn't worth it. Bram watches them go. Then he looks at you as if you've done something he can't file. "Don't make it weird," he says. He walks the first-year back to the castle himself.
> right: Run for a professor
  alignment +tiny
  rel bram +tiny
  say: You bring Brask at a run. By the time you get there it's over: Bram has a split lip and the first-year is fine. He doesn't say thank you. He doesn't give you a demerit that week, either.

@event bram_fathers_shadow
title: His Father's Shadow
pool: rivals_bram_social_routine
tone: tense
when: (bond(bram) == "rival" or bond(bram) == "nemesis") and year >= 2
art: shield
scene: A big man in an old-fashioned prefect's pin standing in the entrance hall with a student who looks smaller than usual, another student watching from the stairs.
text: There's a big man in the entrance hall with Bram's jaw, talking to Bram in a low steady voice. Bram is standing very straight and getting smaller. Then the man sees you on the stairs. "Is that the one?" he says. "The one beating you?"
> left: Walk on as if you didn't hear
  learn bram.father
  rel bram +small
  say: You keep walking. Behind you, Bram says nothing at all. That evening he finds you, and stands there, and says, "You didn't hear that." "Hear what?" you say. He nods once and goes.
> right: Tell his father he's the best prefect here
  learn bram.father
  alignment +tiny
  rel bram +medium
  mood -tiny
  say: The man looks at you as if a chair had spoken. Bram looks at you as if you've hit him. Later, he finds you. "Why," he says. Not a question. You shrug. He gives you no demerits for a month, and never says why either.

# ---------------- Corvin, soured ----------------

@event corvin_locked_out
title: Locked Out
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: corvin
when: rel(corvin) <= -12
weight: 9
art: key
tags: rival
scene: A dormitory door with a new padlock on it, a lanky student leaning beside it and spinning a key on one finger.
text: There's a new padlock on your door. Corvin is leaning beside it, spinning a key on one finger. "Funny thing," he says. "Locks. They don't care whose side you're on. Make it worth my while."
> left: Pay him off
  gold -small
  rel corvin +small
  say: He takes the coins, unlocks the door and bows you in. "Pleasure doing business," he says. He sounds tired, not pleased. The padlock is gone in the morning.
> right: Pick it yourself
  challenge deceive journeyman:
    win:
      guile +small
      rel corvin +tiny
      say: You pick it in four minutes with two hairpins. Corvin watches, and stops spinning the key. "Huh," he says. "Huh." It's the first thing he's said to you in a month that isn't a joke.
    lose:
      mood -small
      rel corvin -tiny
      say: You can't. He lets you struggle for twenty minutes, then unlocks it without a word and walks off. It's worse than if he'd laughed.

@event corvin_bad_odds
title: Bad Odds
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: corvin
when: rel(corvin) <= -12 and renown >= 10
weight: 8
art: mask
tags: rival
scene: A chalked odds board in a dim corner of the common room, a student's name on it with long odds against them, a lanky bookmaker taking coins.
text: Corvin is running a book on you: whether you'll fail Friday's mock paper. The odds aren't flattering. Half the common room has a coin on it. He catches your eye across the room and raises the chalk, as if to say: well?
> left: Bet on yourself
  hint: A wager on the mock: study for it.
  gold -small
  rel corvin -tiny
  challenge research journeyman:
    win:
      gold +medium
      study +small
      say: You put your coin on yourself, at his long odds. Then you study like you've never studied. You pass the mock. Corvin pays out, every coin, and says, "Fine. I'll stop." He doesn't quite, but he shortens the odds.
    lose:
      study +tiny
      say: You put your coin on yourself and study all week. You pass, by one mark under his line. Corvin keeps your coin and chalks the result up with a flourish. "Close," he says. "Closer than the odds."
> right: Shrug it off
  mood -small
  rel corvin +tiny
  say: You let it go. The book runs for a week and closes. Corvin wipes the board clean himself and doesn't start another. He nods to you after, which is something.

# ---------------- Ilse, soured ----------------

@event ilse_frost_door
title: Frost on the Door
class: routine
tone: eerie
trigger: social
actor: ilse
when: met(ilse) and rel(ilse) <= -12
weight: 8
art: snow
tags: rival
scene: A dormitory door completely sealed in clear ice, a student with a kettle staring at it, a single word scratched into the frost.
text: Your door is sealed in ice, a hand thick, clear as glass. Someone has scratched a word into the frost: a Northern word you don't know. It doesn't sound kind. In the village, they say, a girl in white furs bought nothing today, and smiled.
> left: Thaw it the slow way
  health -tiny
  study -tiny
  say: Kettle after kettle. It takes all evening. When the last of it goes, the Northern word goes with it. You never find out what it meant, which might be the point.
> right: Go and find her
  rel ilse +small
  mood -tiny
  say: You find her by the frozen pond. "Your door," you say. She looks at you without blinking. "Your fault," she says. Then, after a long time, "It was a stupid word. I take it back." The ice is gone when you get home.

@event ilse_contempt
title: Beneath Her
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: ilse
when: met(ilse) and rel(ilse) <= -12
weight: 8
art: snow
tags: rival
scene: A girl in white furs walking past another student in the village square without looking, a gust of snow following her that soaks the other student's shoes.
text: Ilse walks past you in the village square as if you were weather. Her private storm, by accident or not, empties itself into your shoes. Two villagers laugh. She doesn't look back.
> left: Say her name
  rel ilse +small
  renown -tiny
  say: She stops. She doesn't turn round. "What," she says. You don't have an answer. Neither does she. But the storm over her head thins, just a little, before she goes.
> right: Let it go
  mood -small
  say: You squelch home. It's the kind of small cold that lasts all day.
